---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Note from "../../components/Note.astro";
const title = "interwingularity — the dysfunctional executives";
---
<BaseLayout {title}>
  <article class="container">
    <h1>interwingularity</h1>
    <p>interwingularity (a term from note-taking philosophy) is the practice of creating links between ideas. instead of siloed knowledge (facts about economics, separate facts about psychology), you build a web where economics ideas connect to psychology concepts. this mirrors how your brain actually works and makes knowledge more retrievable and useful.</p>

    <ul>
      <li>as you learn, ask: "what does this connect to in my existing knowledge?"</li>
      <li>draw diagrams showing how ideas relate (mind maps, concept maps)</li>
      <li>use tools like obsidian or roam to physically link ideas</li>
      <li>revisit old notes and add new connections as you learn more</li>
      <li>surprising connections = deeper understanding</li>
    </ul>

    <Note variant="try">take three random ideas from three fields. spend 10 minutes finding how they might connect or inform each other.</Note>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
